<% content_for :title, t("playlist.home_title") %>

<%# Immersive home, but the music waits to be asked for.
    auto_start was true so the page began playing on load, which is music you
    did not choose coming out of a tab you may not be looking at. It is hard to
    stop for the same reason it is hard to find: the transport bar is not on
    this surface, so the only control is closing the tab, and the operator spent
    a while hunting a MacBook for the source of a Madlib track.
    The tunnel still draws, breathes and blinks on load. Only the audio waits,
    and the controller already starts it on the first pointer or key event, so
    it costs one gesture rather than a hunt. %>
<%= render "playlist/playlists/radio_tunnel", minimal: true, auto_start: false %>
